Z||000011||rogergarrison||03-14-2001||10:03 AM||||some of these cars require special wires, nothing else will work. Some Ferraris have a boot thats 6'' long to reach down thru valve cover and a plug that seals it so it dont fill with water. Thered be no way to get any other kind in there. I never seen a Maserati bi turbo engine though.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by rodmcneill:<BR><B>Anyone who would pay $500.00 for plug wires has to be nuts. Most of the bigger speed shops sell bulk spark plug wires, ends and boots. Various colors and diameters available and probably higher grade wires than the originals. I run Taylor wires on both of my GT's and have been very pleased. Making up your wires for length is very simple.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>||||reg||1
Z||000012||Jay||03-14-2001||10:53 AM||||Maserati is coming back to the US this year with the 3200.  Yes parts are expensive for Maseratis if you go to Ferrari to get them.  Remember Ferrari, Maserati, Lancia, Alfa Romeo and Fiat are all the same company.  Alot of parts are interchangeable.  The secret is to know guys that deal with Italians.  I found that they know what parts are going to work from other cars.  Example?  Why pay $1000 for a Maserati alternator when a $100 Fiat alternator has the same part number.  In short I'd say be different and do it!!!  After all Sergio Pininfarina named the Fiero.  It should have some Italian heart beating under it's skin.||||reg||1
Z||000013||1FST2M6||03-14-2001||11:34 AM||||I've got a 92 Alfa Romeo 164L. and yeah Plug wires are purchased EACH and are more then $70ea. but a N/A 3litre that lays down BONE stock 243hp at the wheels is one HELL-ov-a car. Maserati is the same way.. quirky and strange but stoopid fast.. more reliable them most people think.. their only down-fall is parts avaiability. the $ things really isn't all that bad... you just have to learn to wait for parts. and get used to a timing belt change ever 20-24k miles (Alfas eat belts like theres no tomorrow... they all do! well up to 94... the 156 and 166 don't) and the beautiful purr of nearly any Itialian V6+ or turbo engine just soothes your sole.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg">    <BR>if i only had a pencil thin mustache<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 03-14-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000014||Slammed Fiero||03-14-2001||11:47 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 1FST2M6:<BR><B>I've got a 92 Alfa Romeo 164L.  but a N/A 3litre that lays down BONE stock 243hp at the wheels is one HELL-ov-a car. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>the SAE book I have lists the 92 164L @ 183hp<BR>So does Car test <P>..243 Hp @ the wheels From a NA 3.0ltr??? a 3.0ltr 300zx TWIN TURBO motor puts out 267 @ the wheels , and is far more advanced than the alfa motor.<P>JM<P>||||reg||1
Z||000015||bHooper||03-14-2001||01:05 PM||||my best friend, Paul, had a european eddition 1976 Peugeot 604 (in 1985).  beautifull car, 4 door, metalic chocolotte paint, leather, pwr roof, yadda yadda yadda.  anyway, this car had a Maseratti v-6 racing engine.  the intake, on the carb was big enough you could stick your head in it!<P>man, was that car fast!  we used to go pick on all the "good 'ol boys" in their redneck racers (nothing wrong with cuddas and cameros, but you know what i mean), all jacked up in the back, etc.  <P>we would pull up beside them, at a light, all quite not doing anything... give them the look, while there over there burning gallons and gallons of gas, blap blub blub blub, camming the car to death.  <P>when the light would turn green, we would give them a nice, tractionless lead on us, and then drop it.  lets just say it was always the same at the next light, redneck racer at a slow quiet idle, and Paul reving the Maseratti like a motorcycle!<P>man what a beautifull sound that car made!<P>but yes, parts are expensive, and hard to come by.  he wound up selling it, because the stupid french people wouldn't send him a new altenator.  quote: "what are you silly americans doing with this car?  this car not ment for you! this car to go for america!"<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||1
