Z||000017||N_Man||03-14-2001||08:00 PM||||This thread is so up my alley...<P>My first car a Merkur XR4TI, not to fast stock (my fiero would kill a stock one any day) but a few easy mods liek a header, full 3 inch exaust, and larger air meter. That will give close to 250hp maybe 275tq very easy and reliable... But that wouldn't come close to the slightly modded bi-turbo.<P>Umm the alfa 164 has a freaking powerfull 3.0 liter, i have no clue about the actual HP values but it will easily pull away from the fiero once were moving.  The technology in the alfa V6 all depends on the 164 you get There are 2 engines one is a SOHC ie. 2 cams total and the nicer motor is a DOHC engine which i believe has variable valve timing (dont quote me on that but my dad insists that alfa was the first car manufacturer to do this so i gotta assume).<P>Travis what are you using for plug wires? because $70 each really doesnt sound right.||||reg||1
